cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "MVA Hackathon 2026: from a child's genome to drug hypotheses"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline for the Rare Disease, Real Kid: MVA Hackathon 2026. Track 1 ranks
  candidate variants from whole-genome sequencing; Track 2 derives the disease
  mechanism (NMD, ESM-2, AlphaFold structure, ClinVar validation) and screens
  approved medicines by desired direction of action, with a variant atlas for
  every gene that causes a related disease.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marin Martinez
    given-names: Santiago
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/smarin00/mva-hackathon-2026"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
keywords:
  - rare disease
  - mosaic variegated aneuploidy
  - BUB1B
  - drug repurposing
  - variant interpretation
